  "_about": "Guessing where a model's trucks and couplers are (trains design 3.3, Phase 6): web packages/parts-catalog/src/track/stockGuess.ts, desktop src/track/StockGuess.cpp; both keep `parts` word for word and both run every vector. Input: the model's parts as each app's LDraw reader flattens them (`model`, a file here, or `refs`), each part's origin seen from above in studs (x, y = -LDraw z, y down), the model's footprint `bounds` and the picture's middle `centre` in the same frame. The long side of `bounds` is the car's length; quarterTurns 1 turns the picture clockwise so it runs along x, the front (+) to the right. A part's id is its file name without folders or .dat, lower case; an entry ending in * is a prefix. Bogie plates and motors are the trucks' pivots: when they make two or more clusters (parts within clusterGap studs along the car of each other), the outermost two are the trucks; else wheel parts' clusters; else a quarter of the length in from each end. Couplers: the outermost two coupler parts, when at least minCouplerSpan apart, give the length (body 2 studs shorter); else the body is the footprint and the length 2 studs more. Every number is rounded to 1/100 stud. trucks are [front, rear], studs from the picture's middle along the car. The three .mpd files are from the LDraw Official Model Repository (author TotalyWicked), redistributable under CCAL 2.0.",
